-- busted configuration.
--
-- The suite runs on LuaJIT, which implements Lua 5.1 *runtime semantics* -- the
-- same the client runs -- so behaviour that differs between 5.1 and later versions
-- is caught here. What it does NOT catch is syntax: LuaJIT also accepts a few 5.2
-- constructs (`goto`, labels) and extensions of its own that the client would
-- reject at load time. Treat that as the known gap, not as covered. The interpreter
-- is not forced here: busted was installed into the Lua 5.1 rock tree, so its
-- launcher already execs LuaJIT with the right package paths. `harness_spec.lua`
-- asserts _VERSION, so a wrong interpreter fails the suite instead of passing quietly.
return {
  default = {
    ROOT = { "Ascent/test" },
    pattern = "_spec%.lua$",
    helper = "Ascent/test/helper.lua",
    verbose = true,
  },
}
